    <h2>Operations we do here</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Spays and neuters for dogs, cats and rabbits.</li>
        <li>Lump and skin mass removals, with laboratory testing.</li>
        <li>Wound repairs and abscess treatment.</li>
        <li>Bladder stone removal and other abdominal soft-tissue surgery.</li>
        <li>Eyelid and ear surgery, and dental surgery.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Complex orthopaedic surgery, such as cruciate ligament repair, is referred to a specialist surgeon we trust, and we stay involved before and after.</p>
    <h2>How we keep surgery safe</h2>
    <p>Every patient has a check and, for most, a pre-anaesthetic blood test. A registered nurse monitors heart rate, breathing, blood pressure, oxygen and temperature from the moment of sleep until your pet is sitting up. Patients lie on heated pads, get intravenous fluids, and recover in a quiet ward with a soft bed and someone close by.</p>
    <p class="callout">You get a written estimate before the day, and a phone call from the vet as soon as your pet is awake.</p>
    <h2>Going home</h2>
    <p>At collection a nurse goes through the wound, the medicine, how to keep your pet calm, and what is normal and what is not. You will have our number, and the after-hours number, on the discharge sheet.</p>
